nodecode-hostyourai is a rewrite of cogitor's cogitor/hermes-hostyourai:

  https://github.com/cogitor/hermes-hostyourai
  commit e86d5bf242166cb53dd0362cf960d91e7741194a
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Emil Varga (LICENSE)

The provider row and its alias, the `hyai/auto` model, the task and policy
vocabulary, the `hyai` object in the body and the X-HYAI-Task / X-HYAI-Policy
headers, the System One question that `task auto` classifies a message with,
the balance reading and the /hyai grammar are the plugin's, rewritten in
Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract. Left out: the plugin's own
config plumbing (its ctx and CONFIG_KEY, which the cell's section declaration
replaces); the private-chat gate on the balance, which a Nodecode slash
command does not need; its redirect-refusing opener, since a cell asks through
Nodecode's own HTTP seam; and the bundled hyai-decide skill with
decision_client.py, whose typed-decision calls the nodecode-typesafe cell
already gives Nodecode users.
